Use case: stylized-concept. Production GAME VFX SPRITESHEET, one coherent top-down celestial NOVA IMPACT explosion animation for a purple cosmic tower defense game. Create a transparent wide PNG atlas, exactly FOUR columns by TWO rows, eight equal rectangular cells, read left to right then top row to bottom row. Each cell contains exactly ONE centered circular energy burst, seen straight from above, at exactly the same center inside its cell. Leave at least 12% transparent margin inside EVERY cell, no overlap between cells. Each effect's maximum physical diameter must fit inside its own cell. Genuine transparent alpha, no black/colored backing, no checkerboard, no labels, no border or text. 
Eight consecutive animation frames with a CLEAR phase evolution, not eight identical circles:
1) compact white-blue stellar impact spark with very small violet corona;
2) sharp blue-white star flash and forming thin violet shockwave;
3) compressed star exploding outward, radiant cyan filaments and violet nebula wisps;
4) full ring burst with a white-blue core and rich purple nebula petals, readable open spaces, NOT a solid opaque sphere;
5) peak energy bloom, expanding cyan-violet ring, core already softening;
6) dissipating ring breaking into small crystal stardust particles, weak center;
7) sparse fading blue-violet wisps and a few tiny lingering stars, mostly transparent;
8) extremely faint scattered stardust, almost gone.
Style: polished hand-painted fantasy sci-fi game effect, crisp bright center and controlled soft luminous edges, dominant blue, violet, purple, bright white. No orange fire, no smoke wall, no huge opaque glow disc. Keep restrained enough not to hide enemy sprites. Clean silhouette and readable phase progression when rendered at roughly 128 pixels in-game. ALL visual elements stay within each cell. This is a spritesheet import asset, NOT a poster, illustration board, or UI layout.
